From 449128a65387b7dfb425450cc540b30d9579c6fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Reilly <jreilly1821@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 04:46:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Typing notices and read receipts over federation

Adds the two ephemeral data units a room needs to feel live: typing
notices and read receipts. Both are accepted on the client-server API,
fanned out to every member server as EDUs through the same durable
outbox that carries to-device messages, applied on receipt, and served
through the sliding-sync `typing` and `receipts` extensions, which wake
a waiting long-poll when they change.

- `PUT /rooms/{room_id}/typing/{user_id}` (403 for anyone but the
  sender) and `POST /rooms/{room_id}/receipt/{receipt_type}/{event_id}`.
  Only `m.read` is federated; private receipts stay local.
- `EphemeralState`: per-room typing with a bounded expiry (30s default,
  120s cap) and forward-only read receipts, versioned so sliding sync
  can tell whether anything changed since it started waiting.
- Inbound `m.typing` and `m.receipt` EDUs applied from `/send`.
- Sliding sync fills `extensions.typing.rooms` (excluding the caller)
  and merges real receipts into `extensions.receipts.rooms`, and treats
  a change in either as data when the extension is enabled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
